<Base title="About" current="about" description="About junipernine: operations leadership, bespoke software and the way I work with AI.">
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p>
    I've spent 40 years in operations, leading incident management, site reliability, application
    support and knowledge management across Unix, macOS and AWS cloud environments. My approach is to
    get things right first time: make them stable, measure them, and leave the team able to keep
    them running.
  </p>

  <p>
    I'm now semi-retired from my full-time role, and I'm starting a new chapter. I build bespoke
    software for people and businesses, from personal tools to operational systems. I'm also open to
    consultancy in incident management, operational readiness, cloud cost optimisation and
    observability, where the right opportunity comes along.
  </p>

  <h2>How I work</h2>

  <p>
    I'm fully up to date with AI tooling and comfortable building with it. I use it to plan, build
    and test software, which lets me move quickly without cutting corners on quality.
  </p>

  <p>
    I put guardrails in place from the start: clear limits on what each part of a system can access,
    sensible defaults, and checks that catch problems before users do. Having spent years responding
    to incidents, I design for the day something goes wrong, not just the day it goes right.
  </p>

  <p>
    I work well under pressure, communicate clearly with senior leaders, suppliers, customers and
    engineers alike, and bring a strong eye for detail and for the bigger picture.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a class="button" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/anthony.juniper-nine" rel="me">Connect on LinkedIn</a>
  </p>
</Base>
